<title>GERMANY: Pan-German August cpi inflation falls to 1.4 pct.</title>
<headline>Pan-German August cpi inflation falls to 1.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> GERMAN CPI INFLATION		 Aug 96     July 96     Aug 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)	 -0.1	  +0.3	 +0.1</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr change (pct)		 +1.4	  +1.6	 +1.7</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		    116.9	 117.0	115.3</p>
<p> FINAL WEST GERMAN CPI INFLATION  Aug 96     July 96     Aug 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)	 -0.1 (-0.1) +0.4	 -0.2</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr change (pct)		 +1.4 (+1.4) +1.3	 +1.5</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		    114.5	 114.6	112.9</p>
<p> EAST GERMAN CPI INFLATION	  Aug 96     July 96     Aug 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)	 -0.1	  +0.2	 +1.1</p>
<p> Year-on-year			    +1.8	  +3.0	 +1.7</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		    136.0	 136.1	133.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Previously announced data in brackets.</p>
<p>The Office gave the following details:</p>
<p>					    Mth/mth	     Yr/yr</p>
<p>				     Aug 96  July 96   Aug 96  July 96</p>
<p> Food, drink, tobacco	     -0.5    -0.1	+1.1    +0.9</p>
<p> Clothing, shoes		    +0.1    -0.1	+0.7    +0.7</p>
<p> Rents &amp; energy		     +0.1    +0.2	+1.8    +2.7</p>
<p> Of which: rents		    +0.1    +0.2	+2.7    +3.8</p>
<p>	     energy excl. fuel    unch    +0.5	-1.8    -1.9</p>
<p> Furniture, household goods     +0.1    unch	+0.8    +0.7</p>
<p> Health and body care goods     unch    +0.2	+2.3    +2.2</p>
<p> Traffic and news transmission  +0.2    -0.1	+1.9    +1.9</p>
<p> Education, leisure goods	 +0.1    unch	+1.1    +1.1</p>
<p> Personal equipment, others     +0.2    +4.0	+1.1    -0.1</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
